# M14: the paragraph Enter creates never carries "page break before" (CORE-41). "Chapter two." starts page 2; the status line shows the
# caret's page, which stays 2 after Enter at the end and in the middle, and Enter at the start leaves an empty paragraph above that
# is not a break of its own: the text keeps the one break, and the empty paragraph sits at the foot of page 1.
@copy pgbreak.rtf
@open PGBREAK.RTF
down end                        # the end of "Chapter two.", page 2
enter                           # the new paragraph is on page 2, not page 3
x enter                         # and one more
up up home right right right    # into "Chapter two."
enter                           # split: both halves on page 2
bspace                          # joined again
home enter                      # at the start: an empty paragraph above, the text still on page 2
bspace                          # the empty paragraph goes
f10 end enter                   # File > Exit
n                               # without saving
